cufile_python: KvikIO-compatible local file I/O prototype

Public Python frontends are derived from RAPIDS KvikIO v26.10.00,
commit 5530d767aeb55f63db59a7bb64f2745e8061eee5, licensed under Apache-2.0.
Original NVIDIA copyright and SPDX notices are retained in those files.
Source: https://github.com/rapidsai/kvikio/tree/v26.10.00/python/kvikio

The _lib modules here are a new Python implementation, not the original
Cython modules or libkvikio. __init__.py removes libkvikio loading and exports
the selected CuFile APIs. defaults.py and utils.py omit remote settings and
HTTP helpers. The statistics
frontend documents observation by the Python backend.
Local I/O now always requires libcufile. Legacy compatibility/fallback settings
are retained as no-ops for I/O routing. The Python POSIX/staging backend is
removed; registration always calls cuFile and bounce_buffer_free returns zero.
Buffer/defaults/file/statistics docstrings document these intentional differences.
The import package is renamed to cufile_python, including internal imports.
compat.py provides opt-in aliases for the supported legacy kvikio module names.
batch.py adds an original Python Batch/BatchOp/BatchCompletion interface over
native cuFile batch APIs. This extension has no KvikIO 26.10 Python equivalent.
VERSION and GIT_COMMIT identify the compatibility source, not a released
distribution or the revision of this experimental backend.

No original libkvikio binaries or C++ sources are included.

The archive retains historical local-I/O performance evidence. The unrelated
package-wide experiment and bundled benchmark modules have been removed.
Upstream application helpers are fetched as validation fixtures, outside the
runtime import package.
